# Lets GitHub show a "Cite this repository" button and gives the project a
# stable, machine-readable citation. It is also what Zenodo reads when a release
# is archived to mint a DOI.
#
# The name matches the other CITATION.cff files in these projects. The site uses
# "Dan" as a display byline, which is a separate thing from a citation name.
cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Tradeski — a real-time financial analytics platform for retail investors"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Daniel
    family-names: Lichtenberger
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Danny-397/Tradeski"
url: "https://www.tradeski.dev"
abstract: >-
  Tradeski is a streaming market dashboard: live price and indicator charts,
  Federal Reserve macro series, a correlation matrix, a fundamentals screener,
  portfolio risk analytics, news sentiment scored with a finance-augmented
  VADER lexicon, and an LLM assistant over the user's own holdings. The
  technical indicators are implemented on raw NumPy rather than a TA library,
  so their boundary behaviour is tested directly, and the backend degrades to
  an honest recorded snapshot rather than a blank page when a data provider or
  the free-tier host is unavailable.
keywords:
  - financial analytics
  - technical indicators
  - websockets
  - FRED macroeconomic data
  - sentiment analysis
  - portfolio risk
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-10-20"
